Original files kept here for attribution and so the port can be checked
against the source:

- lib/models/workout.dart — sets, sessions, routines, Epley / RTS one-rep math
- lib/state/tools_state.dart — 1RM, BMI, Mifflin–St Jeor, US Navy, plates,
  warm-up, RPE load, DOTS, Wilks, FFMI
- lib/services/exercise_match.dart — exercise name matching
- lib/catalog/exercise_aliases.dart
- lib/catalog/program_templates.dart

The TypeScript port lives in src/lib/gymmane/.
The original muscle analytics are ported in original-muscle-analytics.ts and
the gymmane-* React components. Exact anatomical paths and hit regions are
imported into src/assets/gymmane-body.json without changing their geometry.
The upstream source snapshot for these additions is
3478b4d91f2a68ac6853fdb02d30f0fd35528306, retained in upstream-analytics/:

- lib/catalog/body_svg.dart — anatomical body paths and hit regions
- lib/widgets/body_map.dart — heat ramps and recovery colours
- lib/widgets/muscle_radar.dart — 12-axis monthly muscle balance radar
- lib/screens/progress_screen.dart — map modes and muscle readouts
- lib/state/stats_state.dart — workload and estimated recovery formulas
- lib/state/fit_core.dart — heat thresholds and calendar helpers
- lib/models/workout.dart and lib/models/exercise.dart — source definitions
- lib/theme/app_colors.dart — recovery palette
- test/muscle_map_test.dart — original workload test expectations

The corresponding source, modifications and build scripts must accompany
distribution in a GPL-compliant manner. See docs/gymmane-muscle-parity.md.
The original upstream CREDITS.md is retained with this snapshot as well.
The exercise list in src/lib/gymmane/catalog.ts was extracted from
lib/catalog/exercise_catalog.dart (447 exercises). Exercise coaching steps
and illustration ids were not needed for client tracking and were not copied.
